      "path": "registry/default/components/moon-tile-01/moon-tile-01.css",
      "content": "/* The moon tile, played twice. Prefixed `mt-` and scoped to this block's own\n   classes, so dropping the file into a project touches nothing else.\n\n   The scene keeps the source drawing's night colours in both themes; only the\n   rim follows the page, light grey in light and the source's dark rim in\n   dark. The dark test is Tailwind's own: inside `.dark` unless a nearer\n   `.theme-light` pins the subtree light. */\n\n.mt-root {\n  --mt-sky: #2e314d;\n  --mt-gold: #ffe400;\n  --mt-gold-shade: #fdca00;\n  --mt-violet: #9292dd;\n  --mt-cloud-1: #8080c1;\n  --mt-cloud-2: #7070ab;\n  --mt-cloud-3: #616196;\n  --mt-cloud-4: #515181;\n  --mt-glow: #4f60f6;\n  --mt-glow-strength: 1;\n  --mt-glow-deep: #040b4d;\n  --mt-lift: #000000;\n  --mt-lift-strength: 0.75;\n  --mt-rim-top: #f4f4f7;\n  --mt-rim-bottom: #dcdce6;\n\n  /* One lap and how many a play runs. The component ends the play at the same\n     total, so change both together. */\n  --mt-lap: 3000ms;\n  --mt-laps: 2;\n  --mt-ease-out: cubic-bezier(0.23, 1, 0.32, 1);\n  --mt-ease-rise: cubic-bezier(0.32, 0.72, 0, 1);\n}\n\n.mt-root:where(.dark, .dark *):not(:where(.theme-light, .theme-light *)) {\n  --mt-rim-top: #373535;\n  --mt-rim-bottom: #141313;\n}\n\n.mt-blend {\n  mix-blend-mode: plus-lighter;\n}\n\n.mt-glow ellipse {\n  fill-opacity: var(--mt-glow-strength);\n}\n\n.mt-lift {\n  flood-color: var(--mt-lift);\n  flood-opacity: var(--mt-lift-strength);\n}\n\n/* Hidden until the first play, so the rise is the first time it is seen. */\n.mt-root[data-waiting] .mt-moon {\n  opacity: 0;\n}\n\n/* The moon rises from behind the clouds once, at the start of a play: a long\n   soft ease out, the iOS drawer curve, so it lifts without a jolt and settles\n   slowly into place, faded in over the first part of the climb so it never\n   shows a hard edge below the cloud line. */\n.mt-root[data-playing] .mt-moon {\n  animation: mt-rise 1600ms var(--mt-ease-rise) both;\n}\n\n/* fill-box puts each origin at the shape's own centre instead of the viewBox\n   corner, so the sparkle swells in place. */\n.mt-sparkle {\n  transform-box: fill-box;\n  transform-origin: center;\n}\n\n/* Every animation hangs off `data-playing` and ends on its first frame, so\n   clearing the attribute after a play lands where the play left off. */\n\n/* The banks sway on one lap each, the back one less far and the other way, so\n   the nearer cloud reads as nearer. Each moves only outwards from rest; see the\n   component for why. */\n.mt-root[data-playing] .mt-bank-front {\n  animation: mt-sway-left var(--mt-lap) ease-in-out var(--mt-laps) both;\n}\n.mt-root[data-playing] .mt-bank-back {\n  animation: mt-sway-right var(--mt-lap) ease-in-out var(--mt-laps) both;\n}\n.mt-root[data-playing] .mt-bank-low {\n  animation: mt-settle var(--mt-lap) ease-in-out var(--mt-laps) both;\n}\n\n/* The small cloud waits a beat before it sets off, so it never moves in step\n   with the banks below it. */\n.mt-root[data-playing] .mt-puff {\n  animation: mt-drift var(--mt-lap) ease-in-out var(--mt-laps) both;\n}\n\n/* Two twinkles a lap: a quick dip, then a slower bloom back to full. */\n.mt-root[data-playing] .mt-sparkle {\n  animation: mt-twinkle calc(var(--mt-lap) / 2) ease-in-out\n    calc(var(--mt-laps) * 2) both;\n}\n\n/* The two stars blink half a beat apart, staggered inside their keyframes\n   rather than by a delay, so both rest at full when the play ends. */\n.mt-root[data-playing] .mt-star-violet {\n  animation: mt-blink-early calc(var(--mt-lap) / 2) ease-in-out\n    calc(var(--mt-laps) * 2) both;\n}\n.mt-root[data-playing] .mt-star-gold {\n  animation: mt-blink-late calc(var(--mt-lap) / 2) ease-in-out\n    calc(var(--mt-laps) * 2) both;\n}\n\n.mt-root[data-playing] .mt-glow {\n  animation: mt-breathe var(--mt-lap) ease-in-out var(--mt-laps) both;\n}\n\n.mt-turn {\n  animation: mt-turn 500ms var(--mt-ease-out);\n}\n\n@keyframes mt-rise {\n  from {\n    transform: translateY(16px);\n    opacity: 0;\n  }\n  45% {\n    opacity: 1;\n  }\n}\n\n@keyframes mt-sway-left {\n  50% {\n    transform: translateX(-1.2px);\n  }\n}\n\n@keyframes mt-sway-right {\n  50% {\n    transform: translateX(0.8px);\n  }\n}\n\n@keyframes mt-settle {\n  50% {\n    transform: translateY(0.8px);\n  }\n}\n\n@keyframes mt-drift {\n  0%,\n  15% {\n    transform: translateX(0);\n  }\n  60% {\n    transform: translateX(2.4px);\n  }\n}\n\n@keyframes mt-twinkle {\n  20% {\n    transform: scale(0.82);\n    opacity: 0.55;\n  }\n}\n\n@keyframes mt-blink-early {\n  25% {\n    opacity: 0.4;\n  }\n  50% {\n    opacity: 1;\n  }\n}\n\n@keyframes mt-blink-late {\n  50% {\n    opacity: 1;\n  }\n  75% {\n    opacity: 0.4;\n  }\n}\n\n@keyframes mt-breathe {\n  50% {\n    opacity: 0.8;\n  }\n}\n\n@keyframes mt-turn {\n  from {\n    transform: rotate(0);\n  }\n  to {\n    transform: rotate(-1turn);\n  }\n}\n\n@media (prefers-reduced-motion: reduce) {\n  .mt-root[data-playing]\n    :is(\n      .mt-moon,\n      .mt-bank-front,\n      .mt-bank-back,\n      .mt-bank-low,\n      .mt-puff,\n      .mt-sparkle,\n      .mt-star,\n      .mt-glow\n    ),\n  .mt-turn {\n    animation: none;\n  }\n\n  /* No play ever starts, so the moon must not wait for one. */\n  .mt-root[data-waiting] .mt-moon {\n    opacity: 1;\n  }\n}\n",
      "type": "registry:file",
      "target": "components/moon-tile-01/moon-tile-01.css"
    }
  ],
